commit ed25d6d94a48a97b032966d69e00f46ab5898d52
Author: Kenneth Jiang <kenneth.jiang@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 18 21:20:15 2026 -0800

    JusPrin view takes OrcaSlicer's message windows and puts them in the chat

    In the JusPrin view, OrcaSlicer still opened its own windows on top of
    the app. Switching printer, filament or process with unsaved setting
    changes asked "Transfer or discard changes". A failed printer connection
    opened "Connect <printer> failed!". A printer refusing a print job, a
    failed upload, the network plug-in and plain OrcaSlicer commands opened
    boxes with only OK, often about pages the view hides. Earlier fixes went
    call site by call site and missed some, such as the drop-down inside
    OrcaSlicer's settings window.

    JusPrin now takes these messages at the few places every one of them
    passes, before the window opens, and keeps the reason it was said:

    - A message with only OK goes into the project chat as a failed entry,
      in the active chat or the empty chat panel, and the chat pane opens
      for it. A printer's message is titled with the printer's name as
      JusPrin names it; any other keeps OrcaSlicer's title. A message that
      arrives while the person is on Home waits in the chat. Nothing is
      drawn on the canvas.
    - A message JusPrin already tells is not shown twice: a failed slice
      (the print issues), an answer the printer chat is waiting for, and a
      failed upload, which now ends its own upload entry as failed instead
      of leaving it running.
    - Pickers, the ZIP chooser, questions (including the two-nozzle "copy
      parameters" question) and windows with fields stay the person's. A box
      over another open window, such as the settings window, stays
      OrcaSlicer's, because that is where the person is looking.
    - "Transfer or discard changes", and the unsaved-changes question asked
      before profiles reload, are answered after a version of the project is
      saved: the setting changes are dropped and Version history keeps them.
      Closing a project and switching a profile share this one save-first
      function (ShellController::save_before_dropping_changes). If no
      version can be saved, nothing is closed or switched and the failure is
      reported as an unexpected error.
    - A filament switch saves its version before the filament slot changes,
      so restoring that version brings back exactly the project before the
      switch.
    - Picking another printer or filament in the header posts a chat line
      saying the unsaved setting changes were dropped and which profiles the
      settings now follow. The model reads that line in English, the chat
      shows it in the person's language, and the new strings are in the 22
      JusPrin catalogs, AI translated.
    - The main window refuses a switch to any page but Home, Prepare and
      Project.
    - JusPrin's own windows open through OrcaMessages/OwnDialogs.hpp and are
      never taken.

    Agreed by Kenneth on 2026-11-18: a switch drops unsaved setting changes
    after saving a version, as closing a project does, and every taken
    message goes into the chat. Not agreed, built as a default: a refused
    switch to a hidden page opens nothing in its place.

    The code is in src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/OrcaMessages/. OrcaSlicer's files
    change by four lines, each marked "// JusPrin:" and reached through
    OrcaHooks.hpp: three added lines at the top of GUI_App::show_dialog,
    GUI_App::push_notification and GUI_App::process_network_msg, and the
    existing fork line in GUI::show_error, which now calls report_error_box
    (a file load's error still goes to the file load first). A rebase
    simulated with git merge-tree against v2.5.1 and upstream/main
    conflicts in the same files with and without this change.

    Tests, JusPrinShellHarness:
    - --orca-messages makes OrcaSlicer speak through its real code in each
      of these ways, then checks which window opened, what was taken with
      which cause, and where it was shown. It switches profiles with unsaved
      edits through the header, Home's printer card, the settings window's
      drop-down, the setup wizard and a profile reload, and restores each
      switch from Version history. --classic-messages runs the same cases
      with the taking off and expects OrcaSlicer's windows: "Transfer or
      discard changes" opens 8 times and "Connect ... failed!" once; with
      the taking on, neither opens.
    - Every mode now fails if an OK-only message or an unsaved-changes
      question reached the person, or a printer's message was taken without
      its printer.
    - --printer-menu checks a header printer switch with unsaved edits, a
      switch whose save fails, and the chat line. --printer-setup checks
      failed Bambu connections show no OrcaSlicer box while classic view
      keeps it.
    - On the final tree every mode passes: orca-messages, printer-menu
      (5 runs), printer-setup, default, dialog-routing, print-issues,
      print-issue-readers, task-chat, check-print, reopen-prompt.
    - The project prompt recorder gained a step for the person switching
      printer or filament from the header. With DeepSeek V4 Flash, 5 of 6
      answers after such a switch said it had dropped the AI's earlier
      change. Only English was run.

    Design: docs/HLSD/orca-messages.md. Lesson:
    agent-docs/jusprin/orca-integration-guide.md.

    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M7S3Z6096RWDKJW55CPC1AXM

